{#
  « Activer les notifications ? » — the invitation the installed
  application offers once (ARCHITECTURE.md §8.111, design.md §7.14).

  Two halves decide whether this is ever seen. The server decides whether
  the markup ships at all (Core\Notification\PushInvitationService: signed
  in, VAPID configured, never refused, not on one of the excluded pages);
  the browser decides whether it opens, because "is this page being read
  inside the installed application" is a media query and a per-device
  fact — see /assets/js/push-invitation.js.

  The subscription is created through the same endpoint « Mon compte »
  uses, so there is no second way to subscribe. What closes this dialog
  is a single call to /api/notifications/invitation.

  No <form> around the body and the footer, for §8.95's reason: nothing is
  submitted here, the persistence is a fetch, and a <form> spanning both
  halves of a scrollable modal pushes its footer off a phone's screen.

  The data-vapid-public-key attribute is the same value « Mon compte »
  hands the toggle — a base64url public key, the one part of the VAPID
  pair that is meant to be public (see Core\Notification\
  VapidKeyPairFactory).
#}
{% embed 'partials/modal.html.twig' with {
    id: 'push-invitation-modal',
    title: 'Activer les notifications ?',
    static_backdrop: false,
} only %}
    {% block body %}
        <div data-vapid-public-key="{{ vapid_public_key }}" id="push-invitation-body">
            <p class="mb-3">
                L'application est installée sur cet appareil. Le site peut désormais vous prévenir
                directement ici — un message dans un groupe, un rappel avant une activité, une tâche
                terminée — même quand l'application est fermée.
            </p>
            <p class="text-body-secondary small mb-0">
                Votre appareil vous demandera de confirmer. Vous choisirez ensuite, type par type,
                ce que vous voulez recevoir, et vous pourrez tout couper quand vous le souhaitez
                depuis « Mon compte ».
            </p>

            <output class="text-warning small mt-3 d-none d-block" data-push-invitation-denied>
                Votre appareil a refusé les notifications. Vous pouvez modifier ce choix dans les
                réglages de votre navigateur, puis les activer depuis « Mon compte ».
            </output>
            <p class="text-danger small mt-3 mb-0 d-none" data-push-invitation-error role="alert">
                Une erreur est survenue. Vous pourrez réessayer depuis « Mon compte ».
            </p>
            {# <output> rather than a <p role="status">: the element carries
               the live region natively, which is what reaches a screen
               reader on every device (SonarCloud Web:S6819). `d-block`
               because <output> is inline by default — same pairing as the
               notice above and as « Mon compte ». #}
            <output class="text-success small mt-3 d-none d-block" data-push-invitation-success>
                C'est fait : les notifications arriveront sur cet appareil.
            </output>
        </div>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block footer %}
        <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-2 w-100">
            {# Three buttons rather than one whose label the script
               rewrites: every word a reader sees stays in this file. #}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary w-100" data-push-invitation-enable>
                Activer les notifications
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary w-100 d-none" data-push-invitation-done
                    data-bs-dismiss="modal">Terminé</button>
            {# « Plus tard » is a real answer and not an escape: it is
               recorded, and after it the invitation never comes back —
               which is why the sentence says where to go instead. The
               close cross, Escape and a click on the backdrop all mean
               the same thing and are recorded the same way. #}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-link w-100" data-push-invitation-later
                    data-bs-dismiss="modal">
                Plus tard — je les activerai depuis « Mon compte »
            </button>
        </div>
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
